# ============================================================================
#  windOS Zen — 00-minimal.list.chroot
#  The floor: X.org/Wayland + gdm3 + installer + plumbing.
#  Idle budget for the whole LiveCD session: < 180 MB RSS.
# ============================================================================

# --- display server / input / GL -------------------------------------------
xorg
xserver-xorg-core
xserver-xorg-input-all
xserver-xorg-video-all
mesa-utils

# --- session & greeter ------------------------------------------------------
gdm3

# --- system plumbing --------------------------------------------------------
systemd-sysv
udev
initramfs-tools
dbus-x11
polkitd
gnome-keyring
console-setup
keyboard-configuration
locales
tzdata
sudo
ca-certificates

# --- boot splash: INTENTIONALLY ABSENT ---------------------------------------
# plymouth + plymouth-themes were dropped here (owner decision: verbose boot,
# no splash). This is a plain removal, NOT a mask: nothing we ship hard-depends
# on plymouth. Verified in debian:trixie with live-build's own install flag
# (`apt-get install -o APT::Install-Recommends=false`): the full 64-package set
# resolves cleanly (1142 pkgs) with zero plymouth-family packages.
#
# Gotcha for future edits: `desktop-base` (pulled in by gnome-core) *Recommends*
# `plymouth-label`, which Depends plymouth -> plymouth-themes. live-build installs
# with Install-Recommends=false, so that edge stays cut. Do NOT flip that on, or
# plymouth comes straight back through desktop-base.
# Theme sources are kept in modules/02-plymouth/ for a future opt-in re-enable.

# --- installer (Module 4) ----------------------------------------------------
calamares

# --- networking / sound / power ----------------------------------------------
network-manager
network-manager-gnome
alsa-utils
volumeicon-alsa

# --- firmware that is redistributable (non-free pulled by --firmware-binary) --
firmware-linux-free
